Package: Censored.DF
Title: Distribution Fitting for Left Singly Censored Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Lidong", "Huang", , "ldhuangz@163.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "YOUR-ORCID-ID"))
Description: This app compares the goodness of fitting with Lognormal and
    Gamma distribution. It provides Shaprio-Wilk statistics and P value
    from package ‘EnvStats’. Besides, the app also shows the cumulative
    probability function (CDF) and Q-Q plot fitting. Final decision about
    the data follows Lognormal or Gamma depends on above computing
    results. Generally, larger P value, and closer line to the scatter in
    CDF/Q-Q plot mean the more likely the data follow that distribution.
    After distribution fitting, one can decide the distribution type and
    calculate the conventional sample statistics based on weighting LOD/2
    substitution.
